(* Go+ v0.21.0 grammar delta: literal patterns and scalar matches.

   The complete base grammar is Go plus the declarations and expressions
   in grammar-v0.20.0.ebnf. Pattern gains a literal production, and
   match gains a second scrutinee class (gap program C2b,
   spec/gap-program-design.md).
*)

Pattern      = "_" | int_lit | ConstructorPattern .
ScalarMatch  = "match" Expression "{"
               { "case" ( int_lit [ "if" Expression ]
                        | identifier | "_" ) ":" StatementList }
               "}" .
             (* goml: `| 0 => …`, `| k => …` through the same clauses *)

(*
  ## Exhaustiveness over literals is the decider's judgment

  This is the work the guards-and-literals deferral named. A match over
  an integer scrutinee accepts literal arms; without a binder or '_'
  fallback, the arms must cover 0..k-1 contiguously AND a hypothesis in
  scope must prove scrutinee < k:

      func Name(n nat, 0 p Lt[n, 3]) string {
      	match n {
      	case 0: return "zero"
      	case 1: return "one"
      	case 2: return "two"
      	}
      }

  The same `Lt[n, 3]` that prunes an enum variant proves this match
  total. Without it the refusal names the missing fact. Contiguity is
  required because the decider proves bounds, not disjunctions; a
  gapped literal set needs a fallback arm.

  ## Semantics and lowering

  Literal arms select by equality in order; guards compose (`case 1 if
  n > 0:`); the fallback arm binds (`case k:`) or discards (`case _:`),
  is unguarded, and comes last. A duplicate literal is unreachable.
  The lowering is an if-chain over a once-evaluated temporary, ending
  in a boundary panic when coverage was proved — hypotheses are static
  and plain Go callers are not, the same honesty as every erased
  boundary.

  ## Deliberately later

  Literal patterns inside constructor arguments (`case Cons(0, t):`)
  are C2c — they extend the Maranget universe per column; until then
  the refusal spells the workaround: `case Cons(x, t) if x == 0:`.
  Impossible arms on scalar matches likewise wait; omit the arm —
  coverage is already decided from the hypotheses.
*)
